{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857036539,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d0e952001uSQ3vnLyCO2Tdq","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d0dd4d001i3JO3nacBnGJJQ","type":"tool","id":"call_7cb182105f164b37bf774a68","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml","offset":1301,"limit":520},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1301-1820\n1301:                       skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1302:                   run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1303:                   log: \"Divergent review pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n1304:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1305:             on_error:\n1306:               run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1307:               log: \"Divergent review pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n1308:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1309:           if_existing_terminal_path:\n1310:             run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1311:             log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n1312:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1313:         if_blocked:\n1314:           log: \"Legal-stop gates blocked STOP. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Continuing review.\"\n1315:         if_stuck_recovery:\n1316:           log: \"Stuck detected ({stuck_count} consecutive no-progress). Entering recovery.\"\n1317:           recovery_strategies:\n1318:             - \"Change granularity: file-level → function-level → line-level review\"\n1319:             - \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\"\n1320:             - \"Escalate severity review: re-examine P2 findings for potential P1 upgrades\"\n1321:           pivot_target: \"Pivot to the least-covered dimension (the review dimension with the fewest iteration passes and lowest coverage ratio).\"\n1322:           set:\n1323:             next_dimension: \"RECOVERY: {recovery_strategy}. Least-covered dimension: {least_explored}\"\n1324:             pending_stop_event: \"stuck_recovery\"\n1325:             pending_stop_reason: \"stuckRecovery\"\n1326:             pending_stop_detail: \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\"\n1327:         if_continue:\n1328:           log: \"Iteration {current_iteration}: Continuing. Dimension: {next_dimension}\"\n1329: \n1330:       step_normalize_pause_events:\n1331:         action: \"Rewrite raw pause and recovery events to the frozen STOP_REASONS enum at emission time: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached\"\n1332:         if_pending_pause_event:\n1333:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.pause_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"normalizedStopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelCause\":\"sentinel-file-detected\",\"fromIterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"strategy\":\"await-operator-resume\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"outcome\":\"paused\",\"lineageRef\":\"{session_id}\",\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\"}}'\n1334:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1335:           message: \"Review paused. Delete review/.deep-review-pause to resume.\"\n1336:           reset:\n1337:             pending_stop_event: null\n1338:             pending_stop_reason: null\n1339:             pending_stop_detail: null\n1340:           halt: true\n1341:           release_lock: step_release_lock\n1342:         if_pending_stuck_recovery:\n1343:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.recovery_started\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"dimensionId\":\"{least_explored}\"},\"data\":{\"normalizedStopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"recoveryCause\":\"repeated-no-progress\",\"fromIterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"strategy\":\"{recovery_strategy_code}\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{least_explored}\",\"outcome\":\"recovery-started\",\"lineageRef\":\"{session_id}\",\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"originatingPauseEventId\":\"none\"}}'\n1344:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1345:           reset:\n1346:             pending_stop_event: null\n1347:             pending_stop_reason: null\n1348:             pending_stop_detail: null\n1349:         if_no_pending_event:\n1350:           proceed: true\n1351:         outputs:\n1352:           - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the state log bytes at the moment the pause or recovery row is emitted\"\n1353: \n1354:       step_generate_state_summary:\n1355:         action: \"Generate compact state summary for dispatch context (~200 tokens)\"\n1356:         generate: |\n1357:           STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1358:           Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1359:           Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1360:           Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1361:           Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1362:           Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1363:           {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1364:           Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1365:           Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1366:           Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1367:           Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1368: \n1369:       step_marker_scan:\n1370:         action: \"H-2 loop-prevention guard: scan previous iteration's rendered prompt for nested review marker\"\n1371:         canonical_header: \"DEEP-REVIEW\"\n1372:         nested_marker_pattern: \"^(DEEP-RESEARCH|CODE-REVIEW)$\"\n1373:         algorithm: |\n1374:           if current_iteration > 1:\n1375:             PREV_PROMPT_PATH = \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{previous_iteration}.md\"\n1376:             if file_exists(PREV_PROMPT_PATH):\n1377:               PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE = head -1 of PREV_PROMPT_PATH\n1378:               if PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE matches nested_marker_pattern:\n1379:                 log \"ERROR: nested review loop detected (foreign deep-loop marker found in previous iteration prompt). Aborting.\"\n1380:                 halt with exit code 2\n1381:         note: |\n1382:           False-positive prevention: a review prompt that starts with its own canonical\n1383:           header is this loop's own iteration output, never a nested dispatch; only a\n1384:           foreign marker (DEEP-RESEARCH or CODE-REVIEW) is, so the guard matches\n1385:           nested_marker_pattern rather than the canonical header. Markers appearing in\n1386:           comments or body text are ignored. True-positive triggers only when a previous\n1387:           iteration's rendered prompt literally starts with a foreign deep-loop marker,\n1388:           indicating a nested review dispatch.\n1389: \n1390:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Iteration ───\n1391:       gate_pre_iteration:\n1392:         applies_to: confirm\n1393:         skip_when: \"The operator already approved the next dispatch in this pass through gate_consecutive_failures, gate_divergent_pivot_choice or gate_divergent_pivot_override.\"\n1394:         type: approval_gate\n1395:         purpose: \"Show planned dimension focus and get approval before dispatching agent\"\n1396:         present: |\n1397:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1398: \n1399:           **Dimension**: {next_dimension}\n1400:           **Dimensions Covered**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1401:           **Findings So Far**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1402:           **Last newFindingsRatio**: {last_newFindingsRatio}\n1403:           **Traceability**: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1404:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1405: \n1406:           Options:\n1407:           A) Proceed with this dimension focus\n1408:           B) Change focus to: [user provides new dimension or focus]\n1409:           C) Stop loop and synthesize now\n1410:           D) Cancel entirely\n1411:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1412:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1413:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_dispatch_iteration }\n1414:         on_B: { action: \"Update next_dimension to user's choice\", proceed_to: step_dispatch_iteration }\n1415:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1416:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1417: \n1418:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1419:         action: \"Dispatch @deep-review agent for one review iteration\"\n1420:         dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1421:         dry_run_preview:\n1422:           before_halt:\n1423:             - \"Generate the state summary.\"\n1424:             - \"Render the prompt pack to terminal preview without writing the prompt file.\"\n1425:             - \"Show the selected executor branch and command or native dispatch target that would run.\"\n1426:         pre_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1427:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately before the dispatch starts\"\n1428:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1429:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than dispatch without it.\"\n1430:         post_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1431:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the dispatch returns\"\n1432:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1433:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n1434:         resolve_executor:\n1435:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1436:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1437:         pre_dispatch:\n1438:           generate_summary: |\n1439:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1440:             Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1441:             Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1442:             Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1443:             Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1444:             Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1445:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1446:             Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1447:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1448:             Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1449:             Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1450:           render_prompt_pack:\n1451:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1452:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1453:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1454:             dry_run_output: \"Render in memory and print to terminal preview; do not write output_path.\"\n1455:             variables:\n1456:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1457:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1458:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1459:               max_tool_calls_per_iteration: \"{config.maxToolCallsPerIteration}\"\n1460:               next_dimension: \"{next_dimension}\"\n1461:               review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n1462:               review_scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n1463:               p0_count: \"{p0_count}\"\n1464:               p1_count: \"{p1_count}\"\n1465:               p2_count: \"{p2_count}\"\n1466:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1467:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1468:               review_focus_block: \"{review_focus_block}\"\n1469:               unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"{unfinished_core_protocols_block}\"\n1470:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1471:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1472:               state_paths_findings_registry: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1473:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1474:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1475:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1476:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1477:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native' or dry_run == true\"\n1478:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1479:           args:\n1480:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1481:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1482:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1483:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1484:         branch_on: \"config.executor.kind\"\n1485:         cli_dispatch_args: '--loop-type review --repo-root \"{repo_root}\" --prompt-file \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --packet-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --generation \"{generation}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --model \"{config.executor.model}\" --reasoning-effort \"{config.executor.reasoningEffort}\" --service-tier \"{config.executor.serviceTier}\" --sandbox-mode \"{config.executor.sandboxMode}\" --timeout-seconds \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"'\n1486:         if_native:\n1487:           dispatch:\n1488:             agent: deep-review\n1489:             model: opus\n1490:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1491:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1492:           wait_for_completion: true\n1493:         if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1494:           command: |\n1495:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-deepseek-harness {cli_dispatch_args} --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\"\n1496:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1497:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1498:           wait_for_completion: true\n1499:           notes:\n1500:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness single-executor: builds through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand), so the pinned harness release, the model allowlist and the route, lineage and guards patches stay one source of truth. runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1501:             - \"The harness starts in the artifact directory, never the repository root, with a fresh DSH_HOME outside the checkout. DSH_HOME, DSH_SPEC_FOLDER, SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED and AI_SESSION_CHILD reach the child through dispatchEnv, and the home is removed in a finally block. The event stream is judged and counted, not echoed\"\n1502:             - \"The prompt opens with a REPOSITORY ROOT line, because the prompt pack's paths and gateway call are repo-relative while the harness starts in the artifact directory\"\n1503:             - \"The child timeout is 30 s under the step timeout (at least half of it), so the finally block removes the home before any outer kill\"\n1504:             - \"validateDshCompletion judges a clean exit, so a plugin that did not activate or a missing final event records a crash dispatch_failure\"\n1505:             - \"Fails closed when the harness binary is absent, off its pinned release or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero). A requested cli-deepseek-harness executor never degrades to native\"\n1506:             - \"The command text never names the harness binary as a bare word, because the ancestry recursion guard reads the parent shell's command line\"\n1507:         if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1508:           command: |\n1509:             node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1510:             console.error('cli-mistral-vibe runs only as a fan-out lineage; rerun with --count=2 or a second --executor group, or choose another executor kind');\n1511:             process.exit(2);\n1512:             EOF\n1513:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1514:           wait_for_completion: true\n1515:           notes:\n1516:             - \"Fails closed before any dispatch receipt is written; the pre_dispatch_audit provenance row for the attempted executor remains\"\n1517:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1518:           command: |\n1519:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-claude-code {cli_dispatch_args} --claude-config-dir \"{optional_claude_config_dir}\"\n1520:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1521:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1522:           wait_for_completion: true\n1523:           render_hint:\n1524:             optional_claude_config_dir: |\n1525:               If config.executor.configDir is set and non-null, expand a leading ~ to HOME and bind that path.\n1526:               Otherwise expand to empty string.\n1527:           notes:\n1528:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so claude-code produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1529:             - \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is forwarded through guardContext.env (CLAUDE_ prefix is allowlisted) so account-specific Claude Code routing is preserved\"\n1530:             - \"permission-mode stays acceptEdits (review's existing iteration-write behavior); claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1531:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1532:         if_cli_opencode:\n1533:           command: |\n1534:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-opencode {cli_dispatch_args}\n1535:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1536:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1537:           wait_for_completion: true\n1538:           notes:\n1539:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so opencode produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1540:             - \"Fail closed before dispatch unless the rendered containment sections exist, --dir is an isolated linked worktree, the primary worktree is clean, and current-worktree changes are confined to artifact_dir both by name and after every path component is resolved through symlinks; append the recovery-baseline commit to state_log\"\n1541:             - \"buildLineageCommand returns empty input, so stdin is closed (EOF), equivalent to </dev/null\"\n1542:             - \"buildLineageCommand receives the route-proof preamble + iteration body as its message\"\n1543:             - \"buildLineageCommand maps reasoningEffort to the installed OpenCode version's supported option\"\n1544:             - \"buildLineageCommand resolves the OpenCode binary and version-correct argv for the configured sandboxMode\"\n1545:             - \"cli-opencode self-invocation guard: this single-executor branch must only run from a non-OpenCode dispatch surface (Claude Code/raw shell). Explicit parallel-detached cli-opencode fan-out is handled by step_fanout_spawn_cli/fanout-run.cjs, not this branch. the `cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode` mode's SKILL.md (`.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md`) §SELF-INVOCATION PROHIBITED contract is the authoritative gate\"\n1546:         if_cli_codex:\n1547:           command: |\n1548:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-codex {cli_dispatch_args}\n1549:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1550:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1551:           wait_for_completion: true\n1552:           notes:\n1553:             - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1554:             - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1555:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1556:             - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1557:             - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1558:             - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1559:         if_cli_cursor:\n1560:           command: |\n1561:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-cursor {cli_dispatch_args}\n1562:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1563:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1564:           wait_for_completion: true\n1565:           notes:\n1566:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1567:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1568:         if_cli_devin:\n1569:           command: |\n1570:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-devin {cli_dispatch_args}\n1571:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1572:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1573:           wait_for_completion: true\n1574:           notes:\n1575:             - \"cli-devin single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-devin model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1576:             - \"Fails closed when devin is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-devin executor never degrades to native\"\n1577:         if_cli_pi:\n1578:           command: |\n1579:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-pi {cli_dispatch_args}\n1580:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1581:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1582:           wait_for_completion: true\n1583:           notes:\n1584:             - \"cli-pi single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-pi model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1585:             - \"Fails closed when pi is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-pi executor never degrades to native\"\n1586:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness has its own single-executor branch, if_cli_deepseek_harness above, built through the same buildLineageCommand. Fan-out also runs the kind\"\n1587:         post_dispatch_validate:\n1588:           validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1589:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type review --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1590:           command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|iteration_verdict_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing|executor_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. executor_missing means the config names a non-native executor and neither the iteration record nor its iteration_start row names one. In a fan-out lineage it means the lineage's invocation-metadata.json does not name that executor. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof + executor contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1591:           assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1592:           assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1593:           assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, mode, run, status, focus, dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsCount, findingsSummary, findingsNew, findingDetails, newFindingsRatio, sessionId, generation, lineageMode, timestamp, durationMs]\n1594:           route_proof:\n1595:             mode: review\n1596:             target_agent: deep-review\n1597:             agent_definition_loaded: true\n1598:             resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\"\n1599:           dispatchReceipt:\n1600:             receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1601:             dispatchId: \"review-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}\"\n1602:           sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1603:           assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n1604:           assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1605:           assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n1606:           failure_reasons:\n1607:             - iteration_file_missing\n1608:             - iteration_file_empty\n1609:             - jsonl_not_appended\n1610:             - jsonl_missing_fields\n1611:             - jsonl_parse_error\n1612:             - jsonl_wrong_type\n1613:             - delta_file_missing\n1614:             - delta_file_empty\n1615:             - delta_file_missing_iteration_record\n1616:             - executor_missing\n1617:             - dispatch_failure_logged\n1618:             - v2_missing_ledger\n1619:             - v2_uncited_ledger_row\n1620:             - v2_broken_linked_finding\n1621:             - v2_shallow_finding_details\n1622:             - delta_iteration_id_mismatch\n1623:             - state_delta_iteration_mismatch\n1624:             - route_proof_missing\n1625:             - route_proof_mismatch\n1626:           warning_surface:\n1627:             source: \"result.warnings\"\n1628:             action: \"emit schema_advisory canonical conflict event\"\n1629:             severity: \"advisory\"\n1630:             event_shape: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"schema_advisory\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"warnings\":{result.warnings},\"severity\":\"advisory\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n1631:             note: \"Warnings do not fail dispatch. Hard failures still emit schema_mismatch through on_failure.\"\n1632:           on_failure:\n1633:             action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n1634:             redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error (per step_evaluate_results.on_missing_outputs) and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n1635:         record_executor_audit:\n1636:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native'\"\n1637:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#appendExecutorAuditToLastRecord\"\n1638:           args:\n1639:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1640:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1641:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1642: \n1643:       step_evaluate_results:\n1644:         action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n1645:         verify:\n1646:           - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1647:           - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n1648:           - strategy_updated: \"Strategy.md has been modified\"\n1649:         extract:\n1650:           - newFindingsRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1651:           - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1652:           - severity_counts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record (P0, P1, P2)\"\n1653:           - dimensions: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1654:           - files_reviewed: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1655:           - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1656:           - reviewed_artifacts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1657:           - traceability_checks: \"From latest JSONL iteration record when present\"\n1658:         on_missing_outputs:\n1659:           action: \"Inspect the latest dispatch record before handling missing outputs\"\n1660:           read:\n1661:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1662:           extract:\n1663:             - last_record: \"Parse the latest state.jsonl record after dispatch\"\n1664:           branch_on: \"last_record.type == 'event' AND last_record.event == 'dispatch_failure' AND last_record.executorUnavailable == true\"\n1665:           if_executor_unavailable:\n1666:             set: { reason: \"error\", stopReason: \"error\" }\n1667:             message: \"The {last_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({last_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1668:             halt: true\n1669:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1670:           if_other_failure:\n1671:             action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n1672:           # Canonical iteration record: include sessionId, generation, durationMs so the reducer can\n1673:           # persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n1674:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1675:           # ledger, so a directly appended error row is dropped by the next refresh.\n1676:             command: |\n1677:               GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1678:               [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1679:               EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-iteration-error.XXXXXX\")\"\n1680:               cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1681:               {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"dimensions\":[\"{next_dimension}\"],\"filesReviewed\":[],\"findingsCount\":0,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":0,\"executed\":0,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":0,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"durationMs\":0,\"sessionId\":\"{config.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.generation},\"lineageMode\":\"{config.lineageMode}\"}}\n1682:               DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1683:               node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1684:               RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1685:               rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1686:               exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1687: \n1688:       step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication:\n1689:         action: \"Validate typed claim-adjudication packets for any new P0/P1 findings and persist the result to state.jsonl so the next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate can read it\"\n1690:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1691:         verify:\n1692:           - typed_packets_present: \"Every new P0/P1 finding in review/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md contains a claim-adjudication JSON block\"\n1693:           - packet_fields: \"Each packet includes claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger\"\n1694:           - missing_packet_ids: \"List of new P0/P1 finding IDs that are missing a typed packet or field; empty array when all packets validate\"\n1695:         on_pass:\n1696:           set:\n1697:             claim_adjudication_passed: true\n1698:           # The row is staged as a canonical ledger event and appended by the gateway:\n1699:           # the state log is a projection of the ledger, so a write beside it is dropped\n1700:           # by the next refresh.\n1701:           command: |\n1702:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1703:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1704:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1705:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1706:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":[],\"reason\":null,\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1707:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1708:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1709:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1710:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1711:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1712:           log: \"Claim adjudication passed for iteration {current_iteration}. All new P0/P1 findings have typed packets.\"\n1713:         on_fail:\n1714:           action: \"Mark the iteration as invalid for convergence. The next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate (step_check_convergence step 0) reads the persisted `passed: false` event and vetoes STOP until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packets.\"\n1715:           set:\n1716:             claim_adjudication_passed: false\n1717:           command: |\n1718:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1719:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1720:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1721:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1722:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":false,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":{missing_packet_ids},\"reason\":\"Missing typed packet fields for new P0/P1 findings\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1723:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1724:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1725:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1726:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1727:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1728:           log: \"Claim adjudication incomplete for new P0/P1 findings. Event persisted. The next iteration's step_check_convergence claim-adjudication pre-check will veto STOP while `passed: false` remains the latest event and active P0/P1 > 0.\"\n1729: \n1730:       step_reduce_review_state:\n1731:         action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n1732:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1733:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n1734:         read:\n1735:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1736:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1738:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1739:         write:\n1740:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1741:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1742:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1743:         failure_modes:\n1744:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1745:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1746:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1747:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n1748:         note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n1749: \n1750:       step_graph_upsert:\n1751:         action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n1752:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1753:         read:\n1754:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1755:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1756:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1757:         transform: |\n1758:           1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n1759:           2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n1760:           3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n1761:           4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n1762:           5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n1763:           6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n1764:           7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n1765:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}'\"\n1766:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n1767:         outputs:\n1768:           - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n1769:           - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n1770: \n1771:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n1772:       gate_post_iteration:\n1773:         applies_to: confirm\n1774:         type: approval_gate\n1775:         purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n1776:         present: |\n1777:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n1778: \n1779:           **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n1780:           **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n1781:           **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n1782:           **Status**: {status}\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1821]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1301-1820\n1301:                       skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1302:                   run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1303:                   log: \"Divergent review pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n1304:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1305:             on_error:\n1306:               run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1307:               log: \"Divergent review pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n1308:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1309:           if_existing_terminal_path:\n1310:             run_first: record_terminal_gates\n1311:             log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n1312:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1313:         if_blocked:\n1314:           log: \"Legal-stop gates blocked STOP. Failed gates: {blocked_by_csv}. Continuing review.\"\n1315:         if_stuck_recovery:\n1316:           log: \"Stuck detected ({stuck_count} consecutive no-progress). Entering recovery.\"\n1317:           recovery_strategies:\n1318:             - \"Change granularity: file-level → function-level → line-level review\"\n1319:             - \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core or overlay checks\"\n1320:             - \"Escalate severity review: re-examine P2 findings for potential P1 upgrades\"\n1321:           pivot_target: \"Pivot to the least-covered dimension (the review dimension with the fewest iteration passes and lowest coverage ratio).\"\n1322:           set:\n1323:             next_dimension: \"RECOVERY: {recovery_strategy}. Least-covered dimension: {least_explored}\"\n1324:             pending_stop_event: \"stuck_recovery\"\n1325:             pending_stop_reason: \"stuckRecovery\"\n1326:             pending_stop_detail: \"Recovery path activated after repeated no-progress iterations\"\n1327:         if_continue:\n1328:           log: \"Iteration {current_iteration}: Continuing. Dimension: {next_dimension}\"\n1329: \n1330:       step_normalize_pause_events:\n1331:         action: \"Rewrite raw pause and recovery events to the frozen STOP_REASONS enum at emission time: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached\"\n1332:         if_pending_pause_event:\n1333:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.pause_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"normalizedStopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelCause\":\"sentinel-file-detected\",\"fromIterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"strategy\":\"await-operator-resume\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"outcome\":\"paused\",\"lineageRef\":\"{session_id}\",\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\"}}'\n1334:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1335:           message: \"Review paused. Delete review/.deep-review-pause to resume.\"\n1336:           reset:\n1337:             pending_stop_event: null\n1338:             pending_stop_reason: null\n1339:             pending_stop_detail: null\n1340:           halt: true\n1341:           release_lock: step_release_lock\n1342:         if_pending_stuck_recovery:\n1343:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.recovery_started\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"dimensionId\":\"{least_explored}\"},\"data\":{\"normalizedStopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"recoveryCause\":\"repeated-no-progress\",\"fromIterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\",\"strategy\":\"{recovery_strategy_code}\",\"targetDimensionId\":\"{least_explored}\",\"outcome\":\"recovery-started\",\"lineageRef\":\"{session_id}\",\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"originatingPauseEventId\":\"none\"}}'\n1344:           dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n1345:           reset:\n1346:             pending_stop_event: null\n1347:             pending_stop_reason: null\n1348:             pending_stop_detail: null\n1349:         if_no_pending_event:\n1350:           proceed: true\n1351:         outputs:\n1352:           - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the state log bytes at the moment the pause or recovery row is emitted\"\n1353: \n1354:       step_generate_state_summary:\n1355:         action: \"Generate compact state summary for dispatch context (~200 tokens)\"\n1356:         generate: |\n1357:           STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1358:           Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1359:           Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1360:           Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1361:           Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1362:           Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1363:           {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1364:           Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1365:           Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1366:           Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1367:           Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1368: \n1369:       step_marker_scan:\n1370:         action: \"H-2 loop-prevention guard: scan previous iteration's rendered prompt for nested review marker\"\n1371:         canonical_header: \"DEEP-REVIEW\"\n1372:         nested_marker_pattern: \"^(DEEP-RESEARCH|CODE-REVIEW)$\"\n1373:         algorithm: |\n1374:           if current_iteration > 1:\n1375:             PREV_PROMPT_PATH = \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{previous_iteration}.md\"\n1376:             if file_exists(PREV_PROMPT_PATH):\n1377:               PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE = head -1 of PREV_PROMPT_PATH\n1378:               if PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE matches nested_marker_pattern:\n1379:                 log \"ERROR: nested review loop detected (foreign deep-loop marker found in previous iteration prompt). Aborting.\"\n1380:                 halt with exit code 2\n1381:         note: |\n1382:           False-positive prevention: a review prompt that starts with its own canonical\n1383:           header is this loop's own iteration output, never a nested dispatch; only a\n1384:           foreign marker (DEEP-RESEARCH or CODE-REVIEW) is, so the guard matches\n1385:           nested_marker_pattern rather than the canonical header. Markers appearing in\n1386:           comments or body text are ignored. True-positive triggers only when a previous\n1387:           iteration's rendered prompt literally starts with a foreign deep-loop marker,\n1388:           indicating a nested review dispatch.\n1389: \n1390:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Pre-Iteration ───\n1391:       gate_pre_iteration:\n1392:         applies_to: confirm\n1393:         skip_when: \"The operator already approved the next dispatch in this pass through gate_consecutive_failures, gate_divergent_pivot_choice or gate_divergent_pivot_override.\"\n1394:         type: approval_gate\n1395:         purpose: \"Show planned dimension focus and get approval before dispatching agent\"\n1396:         present: |\n1397:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1398: \n1399:           **Dimension**: {next_dimension}\n1400:           **Dimensions Covered**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1401:           **Findings So Far**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1402:           **Last newFindingsRatio**: {last_newFindingsRatio}\n1403:           **Traceability**: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1404:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1405: \n1406:           Options:\n1407:           A) Proceed with this dimension focus\n1408:           B) Change focus to: [user provides new dimension or focus]\n1409:           C) Stop loop and synthesize now\n1410:           D) Cancel entirely\n1411:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1412:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1413:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_dispatch_iteration }\n1414:         on_B: { action: \"Update next_dimension to user's choice\", proceed_to: step_dispatch_iteration }\n1415:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1416:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1417: \n1418:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1419:         action: \"Dispatch @deep-review agent for one review iteration\"\n1420:         dry_run_boundary: \"dispatch\"\n1421:         dry_run_preview:\n1422:           before_halt:\n1423:             - \"Generate the state summary.\"\n1424:             - \"Render the prompt pack to terminal preview without writing the prompt file.\"\n1425:             - \"Show the selected executor branch and command or native dispatch target that would run.\"\n1426:         pre_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1427:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately before the dispatch starts\"\n1428:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1429:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than dispatch without it.\"\n1430:         post_dispatch_refresh_lock:\n1431:           action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the dispatch returns\"\n1432:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n1433:           on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. Run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n1434:         resolve_executor:\n1435:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1436:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1437:         pre_dispatch:\n1438:           generate_summary: |\n1439:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1440:             Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1441:             Dimension: {next_dimension}\n1442:             Prior Findings: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1443:             Dimension Coverage: {dimensions_covered_list} ({dimension_coverage})\n1444:             Traceability: core={core_protocol_status} overlay={overlay_protocol_status}\n1445:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1446:             Coverage Age: {coverage_age}\n1447:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest}\n1448:             Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1449:             Provisional Verdict: {PASS|CONDITIONAL|FAIL|PENDING} hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n1450:           render_prompt_pack:\n1451:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1452:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1453:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1454:             dry_run_output: \"Render in memory and print to terminal preview; do not write output_path.\"\n1455:             variables:\n1456:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1457:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1458:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1459:               max_tool_calls_per_iteration: \"{config.maxToolCallsPerIteration}\"\n1460:               next_dimension: \"{next_dimension}\"\n1461:               review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n1462:               review_scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n1463:               p0_count: \"{p0_count}\"\n1464:               p1_count: \"{p1_count}\"\n1465:               p2_count: \"{p2_count}\"\n1466:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1467:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1468:               review_focus_block: \"{review_focus_block}\"\n1469:               unfinished_core_protocols_block: \"{unfinished_core_protocols_block}\"\n1470:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1471:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1472:               state_paths_findings_registry: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1473:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1474:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1475:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1476:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1477:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native' or dry_run == true\"\n1478:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1479:           args:\n1480:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1481:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1482:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1483:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1484:         branch_on: \"config.executor.kind\"\n1485:         cli_dispatch_args: '--loop-type review --repo-root \"{repo_root}\" --prompt-file \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --packet-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --generation \"{generation}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --model \"{config.executor.model}\" --reasoning-effort \"{config.executor.reasoningEffort}\" --service-tier \"{config.executor.serviceTier}\" --sandbox-mode \"{config.executor.sandboxMode}\" --timeout-seconds \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"'\n1486:         if_native:\n1487:           dispatch:\n1488:             agent: deep-review\n1489:             model: opus\n1490:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1491:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1492:           wait_for_completion: true\n1493:         if_cli_deepseek_harness:\n1494:           command: |\n1495:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-deepseek-harness {cli_dispatch_args} --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\"\n1496:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1497:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1498:           wait_for_completion: true\n1499:           notes:\n1500:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness single-executor: builds through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand), so the pinned harness release, the model allowlist and the route, lineage and guards patches stay one source of truth. runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1501:             - \"The harness starts in the artifact directory, never the repository root, with a fresh DSH_HOME outside the checkout. DSH_HOME, DSH_SPEC_FOLDER, SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED and AI_SESSION_CHILD reach the child through dispatchEnv, and the home is removed in a finally block. The event stream is judged and counted, not echoed\"\n1502:             - \"The prompt opens with a REPOSITORY ROOT line, because the prompt pack's paths and gateway call are repo-relative while the harness starts in the artifact directory\"\n1503:             - \"The child timeout is 30 s under the step timeout (at least half of it), so the finally block removes the home before any outer kill\"\n1504:             - \"validateDshCompletion judges a clean exit, so a plugin that did not activate or a missing final event records a crash dispatch_failure\"\n1505:             - \"Fails closed when the harness binary is absent, off its pinned release or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero). A requested cli-deepseek-harness executor never degrades to native\"\n1506:             - \"The command text never names the harness binary as a bare word, because the ancestry recursion guard reads the parent shell's command line\"\n1507:         if_cli_mistral_vibe:\n1508:           command: |\n1509:             node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1510:             console.error('cli-mistral-vibe runs only as a fan-out lineage; rerun with --count=2 or a second --executor group, or choose another executor kind');\n1511:             process.exit(2);\n1512:             EOF\n1513:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1514:           wait_for_completion: true\n1515:           notes:\n1516:             - \"Fails closed before any dispatch receipt is written; the pre_dispatch_audit provenance row for the attempted executor remains\"\n1517:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1518:           command: |\n1519:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-claude-code {cli_dispatch_args} --claude-config-dir \"{optional_claude_config_dir}\"\n1520:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1521:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1522:           wait_for_completion: true\n1523:           render_hint:\n1524:             optional_claude_config_dir: |\n1525:               If config.executor.configDir is set and non-null, expand a leading ~ to HOME and bind that path.\n1526:               Otherwise expand to empty string.\n1527:           notes:\n1528:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so claude-code produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1529:             - \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is forwarded through guardContext.env (CLAUDE_ prefix is allowlisted) so account-specific Claude Code routing is preserved\"\n1530:             - \"permission-mode stays acceptEdits (review's existing iteration-write behavior); claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1531:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1532:         if_cli_opencode:\n1533:           command: |\n1534:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-opencode {cli_dispatch_args}\n1535:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1536:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1537:           wait_for_completion: true\n1538:           notes:\n1539:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so opencode produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard + env allowlist enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1540:             - \"Fail closed before dispatch unless the rendered containment sections exist, --dir is an isolated linked worktree, the primary worktree is clean, and current-worktree changes are confined to artifact_dir both by name and after every path component is resolved through symlinks; append the recovery-baseline commit to state_log\"\n1541:             - \"buildLineageCommand returns empty input, so stdin is closed (EOF), equivalent to </dev/null\"\n1542:             - \"buildLineageCommand receives the route-proof preamble + iteration body as its message\"\n1543:             - \"buildLineageCommand maps reasoningEffort to the installed OpenCode version's supported option\"\n1544:             - \"buildLineageCommand resolves the OpenCode binary and version-correct argv for the configured sandboxMode\"\n1545:             - \"cli-opencode self-invocation guard: this single-executor branch must only run from a non-OpenCode dispatch surface (Claude Code/raw shell). Explicit parallel-detached cli-opencode fan-out is handled by step_fanout_spawn_cli/fanout-run.cjs, not this branch. the `cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode` mode's SKILL.md (`.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md`) §SELF-INVOCATION PROHIBITED contract is the authoritative gate\"\n1546:         if_cli_codex:\n1547:           command: |\n1548:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-codex {cli_dispatch_args}\n1549:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1550:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1551:           wait_for_completion: true\n1552:           notes:\n1553:             - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n1554:             - \"Nested CLI dispatch from a lineage is a route violation, not a slow path: a codex lineage that runs this script spawns codex inside its own sandbox, where the child cannot initialize and every iteration fails. The script refuses that case before any spawn and before any dispatch receipt is written, exiting RECURSION_GUARD_EXIT_CODE; that refusal is a route error to fix, never a redispatchable executor failure.\"\n1555:             - \"Routed through runAuditedExecutorCommand so codex produces INTENT + COMPLETION dispatch receipts; recursion guard (CODEX_SESSION_ID) + env allowlist (CODEX_/OPENAI_/AZURE_OPENAI_) enforced via buildExecutorDispatchEnv\"\n1556:             - \"Fails closed when the codex binary is absent (exit 1) — parity with the fan-out cli-codex lineage guard in fanout-run.cjs; codex routing never degrades to native\"\n1557:             - \"codex exec reads the iteration prompt from stdin via the trailing '-' (input: promptBody); '-c model_reasoning_effort=' maps reasoning depth, default medium; '-c service_tier=' forwarded when configured\"\n1558:             - \"--sandbox workspace-write is required so the iteration can write its own iteration file/delta/state record (read-only would fail the post-dispatch artifact gate); -c approval_policy=never keeps it non-interactive; --model omitted when unset so ~/.codex/config.toml default applies\"\n1559:         if_cli_cursor:\n1560:           command: |\n1561:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-cursor {cli_dispatch_args}\n1562:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1563:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1564:           wait_for_completion: true\n1565:           notes:\n1566:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1567:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1568:         if_cli_devin:\n1569:           command: |\n1570:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-devin {cli_dispatch_args}\n1571:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1572:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1573:           wait_for_completion: true\n1574:           notes:\n1575:             - \"cli-devin single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-devin model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1576:             - \"Fails closed when devin is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-devin executor never degrades to native\"\n1577:         if_cli_pi:\n1578:           command: |\n1579:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs --executor cli-pi {cli_dispatch_args}\n1580:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1581:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1582:           wait_for_completion: true\n1583:           notes:\n1584:             - \"cli-pi single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-pi model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1585:             - \"Fails closed when pi is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-pi executor never degrades to native\"\n1586:             - \"cli-deepseek-harness has its own single-executor branch, if_cli_deepseek_harness above, built through the same buildLineageCommand. Fan-out also runs the kind\"\n1587:         post_dispatch_validate:\n1588:           validator: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/post-dispatch-validate.ts#validateIterationOutputs\"\n1589:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type review --artifact-dir {artifact_dir} --iteration {current_iteration}\"\n1590:           command_note: \"Mechanical leaf-reliability gate: exit 0 = complete; non-zero prints one machine reason (dispatch_failed|iteration_file_missing|iteration_verdict_missing|state_record_missing|route_proof_missing|route_proof_mismatch|delta_file_missing|executor_missing). dispatch_failed means the narrative is missing and the completion receipt shows a non-zero exit or a signal. executor_missing means the config names a non-native executor and neither the iteration record nor its iteration_start row names one. In a fan-out lineage it means the lineage's invocation-metadata.json does not name that executor. The script enforces the artifact + route-proof + executor contract instead of trusting the leaf to self-report, and a non-zero exit triggers on_failure.redispatch_once.\"\n1591:           assert_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1592:           assert_appended: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1593:           assert_jsonl_fields: [type, iteration, mode, run, status, focus, dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsCount, findingsSummary, findingsNew, findingDetails, newFindingsRatio, sessionId, generation, lineageMode, timestamp, durationMs]\n1594:           route_proof:\n1595:             mode: review\n1596:             target_agent: deep-review\n1597:             agent_definition_loaded: true\n1598:             resolved_route: \"Resolved route: mode=review target_agent=deep-review\"\n1599:           dispatchReceipt:\n1600:             receiptDir: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts\"\n1601:             dispatchId: \"review-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}\"\n1602:           sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1603:           assert_canonical_type: \"iteration\"\n1604:           assert_delta_file_exists: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1605:           assert_delta_file_has_iteration_record: true\n1606:           failure_reasons:\n1607:             - iteration_file_missing\n1608:             - iteration_file_empty\n1609:             - jsonl_not_appended\n1610:             - jsonl_missing_fields\n1611:             - jsonl_parse_error\n1612:             - jsonl_wrong_type\n1613:             - delta_file_missing\n1614:             - delta_file_empty\n1615:             - delta_file_missing_iteration_record\n1616:             - executor_missing\n1617:             - dispatch_failure_logged\n1618:             - v2_missing_ledger\n1619:             - v2_uncited_ledger_row\n1620:             - v2_broken_linked_finding\n1621:             - v2_shallow_finding_details\n1622:             - delta_iteration_id_mismatch\n1623:             - state_delta_iteration_mismatch\n1624:             - route_proof_missing\n1625:             - route_proof_mismatch\n1626:           warning_surface:\n1627:             source: \"result.warnings\"\n1628:             action: \"emit schema_advisory canonical conflict event\"\n1629:             severity: \"advisory\"\n1630:             event_shape: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"schema_advisory\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"warnings\":{result.warnings},\"severity\":\"advisory\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n1631:             note: \"Warnings do not fail dispatch. Hard failures still emit schema_mismatch through on_failure.\"\n1632:           on_failure:\n1633:             action: \"emit schema_mismatch canonical conflict event\"\n1634:             redispatch_once: \"On the FIRST failure of the mechanical command check for this iteration, re-run step_dispatch_iteration exactly once for the same iteration number, then re-run the check. If it still fails, record the iteration as error (per step_evaluate_results.on_missing_outputs) and continue. Never re-dispatch a given iteration more than once.\"\n1635:         record_executor_audit:\n1636:           skip_when: \"config.executor.kind == 'native'\"\n1637:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#appendExecutorAuditToLastRecord\"\n1638:           args:\n1639:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1640:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1641:             sessionId: \"{session_id}\"\n1642: \n1643:       step_evaluate_results:\n1644:         action: \"Verify iteration outputs and extract metrics\"\n1645:         verify:\n1646:           - file_exists: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1647:           - jsonl_appended: \"New iteration record in state.jsonl\"\n1648:           - strategy_updated: \"Strategy.md has been modified\"\n1649:         extract:\n1650:           - newFindingsRatio: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1651:           - findings_count: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1652:           - severity_counts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record (P0, P1, P2)\"\n1653:           - dimensions: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1654:           - files_reviewed: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1655:           - status: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1656:           - reviewed_artifacts: \"From latest JSONL iteration record\"\n1657:           - traceability_checks: \"From latest JSONL iteration record when present\"\n1658:         on_missing_outputs:\n1659:           action: \"Inspect the latest dispatch record before handling missing outputs\"\n1660:           read:\n1661:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1662:           extract:\n1663:             - last_record: \"Parse the latest state.jsonl record after dispatch\"\n1664:           branch_on: \"last_record.type == 'event' AND last_record.event == 'dispatch_failure' AND last_record.executorUnavailable == true\"\n1665:           if_executor_unavailable:\n1666:             set: { reason: \"error\", stopReason: \"error\" }\n1667:             message: \"The {last_record.executor.kind} executor is unavailable ({last_record.matchedMarker}). Switch executor or wait, then resume this run.\"\n1668:             halt: true\n1669:             release_lock: step_release_lock\n1670:           if_other_failure:\n1671:             action: \"Mark iteration as 'error', continue to next\"\n1672:           # Canonical iteration record: include sessionId, generation, durationMs so the reducer can\n1673:           # persist the failure without dropping the iteration. Schema source: state-format.md §Iteration Records.\n1674:           # The row is staged for the append gateway: the state log is a projection of the\n1675:           # ledger, so a directly appended error row is dropped by the next refresh.\n1676:             command: |\n1677:               GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1678:               [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1679:               EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-iteration-error.XXXXXX\")\"\n1680:               cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1681:               {\"stem\":\"deep_review.iteration_error\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":{current_iteration},\"run\":{current_iteration},\"mode\":\"review\",\"status\":\"error\",\"focus\":\"{next_dimension}\",\"dimensions\":[\"{next_dimension}\"],\"filesReviewed\":[],\"findingsCount\":0,\"findingsSummary\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingsNew\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"findingDetails\":[],\"traceabilityChecks\":{\"summary\":{\"required\":0,\"executed\":0,\"pass\":0,\"partial\":0,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"notApplicable\":0,\"gatingFailures\":0},\"results\":[]},\"newFindingsRatio\":0.0,\"durationMs\":0,\"sessionId\":\"{config.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.generation},\"lineageMode\":\"{config.lineageMode}\"}}\n1682:               DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1683:               node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1684:               RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1685:               rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1686:               exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1687: \n1688:       step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication:\n1689:         action: \"Validate typed claim-adjudication packets for any new P0/P1 findings and persist the result to state.jsonl so the next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate can read it\"\n1690:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1691:         verify:\n1692:           - typed_packets_present: \"Every new P0/P1 finding in review/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md contains a claim-adjudication JSON block\"\n1693:           - packet_fields: \"Each packet includes claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger\"\n1694:           - missing_packet_ids: \"List of new P0/P1 finding IDs that are missing a typed packet or field; empty array when all packets validate\"\n1695:         on_pass:\n1696:           set:\n1697:             claim_adjudication_passed: true\n1698:           # The row is staged as a canonical ledger event and appended by the gateway:\n1699:           # the state log is a projection of the ledger, so a write beside it is dropped\n1700:           # by the next refresh.\n1701:           command: |\n1702:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1703:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1704:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1705:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1706:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":true,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":[],\"reason\":null,\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1707:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1708:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1709:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1710:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1711:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1712:           log: \"Claim adjudication passed for iteration {current_iteration}. All new P0/P1 findings have typed packets.\"\n1713:         on_fail:\n1714:           action: \"Mark the iteration as invalid for convergence. The next iteration's claimAdjudicationGate (step_check_convergence step 0) reads the persisted `passed: false` event and vetoes STOP until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packets.\"\n1715:           set:\n1716:             claim_adjudication_passed: false\n1717:           command: |\n1718:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1719:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n1720:             EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-claim-adjudication.XXXXXX\")\"\n1721:             cat <<'DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD' > \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1722:             {\"stem\":\"deep_review.claim_adjudication\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"passed\":false,\"activeP0P1\":{active_p0_p1_count},\"missingPackets\":{missing_packet_ids},\"reason\":\"Missing typed packet fields for new P0/P1 findings\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}}\n1723:             DEEP_LOOP_STATE_RECORD\n1724:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1725:             RECORD_STATUS=$?\n1726:             rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n1727:             exit \"$RECORD_STATUS\"\n1728:           log: \"Claim adjudication incomplete for new P0/P1 findings. Event persisted. The next iteration's step_check_convergence claim-adjudication pre-check will veto STOP while `passed: false` remains the latest event and active P0/P1 > 0.\"\n1729: \n1730:       step_reduce_review_state:\n1731:         action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n1732:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n1733:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n1734:         read:\n1735:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1736:           - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1738:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1739:         write:\n1740:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1741:           - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n1742:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1743:         failure_modes:\n1744:           malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n1745:           missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n1746:           schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n1747:         guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n1748:         note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n1749: \n1750:       step_graph_upsert:\n1751:         action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n1752:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n1753:         read:\n1754:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1755:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1756:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n1757:         transform: |\n1758:           1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n1759:           2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n1760:           3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n1761:           4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n1762:           5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n1763:           6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n1764:           7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n1765:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}'\"\n1766:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n1767:         outputs:\n1768:           - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n1769:           - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n1770: \n1771:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n1772:       gate_post_iteration:\n1773:         applies_to: confirm\n1774:         type: approval_gate\n1775:         purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n1776:         present: |\n1777:           ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n1778: \n1779:           **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n1780:           **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n1781:           **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n1782:           **Status**: {status}\n1783:           **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n1784:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n1785:           **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n1786:           **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n1787: \n1788:           **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n1789:           {last_3_summaries}\n1790: \n1791:           Options:\n1792:           A) Continue to next iteration\n1793:           B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n1794:           C) Stop loop and synthesize\n1795:           D) Cancel entirely\n1796:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n1797:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n1798:         on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1799:         on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n1800:         on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n1801:         on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n1802: \n1803:       step_update_tracking:\n1804:         action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n1805:         set:\n1806:           current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n1807:         log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n1808: \n1809:       step_loop_decision:\n1810:         action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n1811:         goto: step_read_state\n1812: \n1813:   # ════════\n1814:   # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n1815:   # ════════\n1816:   phase_synthesis:\n1817:     purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n1818:     steps:\n1819: \n1820:       step_fanout_merge:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1821]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\",\"offset\":1301,\"limit\":520}"},"time":{"start":1794857036114,"end":1794857036539}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857036542,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d0e757001xN2dStMlxCk8YV","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d0dd4d001i3JO3nacBnGJJQ","type":"tool","id":"call_44e330c741674aa099e6a7e2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md","offset":100,"limit":120},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md, lines 100-219\n100: \n101: | Required Field | Type | Description |\n102: |---------------|------|-------------|\n103: | mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n104: | dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n105: | filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n106: | sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n107: | generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n108: | lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n109: | findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n110: | findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n111: | findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n112: | newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n113: \n114: ### Convergence Signals\n115: \n116: | Signal | Weight | Description |\n117: |--------|--------|-------------|\n118: | rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n119: | madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n120: | dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n121: | compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n122: \n123: **Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n124: \n125: ### Graph Events\n126: \n127: The optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The workflow projects them into graph nodes and edges, and the runtime upsert script (`runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`) persists them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n128: \n129: ```json\n130: {\n131:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n132:   \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n133:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n134:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n135:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n136:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n137:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n138:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n139:   \"generation\": 1,\n140:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n141:   \"graphEvents\": [\n142:     { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n143:     { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n144:     { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n145:     { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n146:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n147:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n148:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n151:   \"durationMs\": 51000\n152: }\n153: ```\n154: \n155: #### Event payload shape\n156: \n157: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n158: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n159: | type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n160: | id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n161: | label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n162: | relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n163: | source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n164: | target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n165: | metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n166: \n167: #### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n168: \n169: `graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n170: \n171: Concrete obligations for producers:\n172: \n173: 1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n174: 2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n175: 3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n176: 4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n177: \n178: The composite key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` enforces this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows survive independently.\n179: \n180: ### Synthesis Event\n181: \n182: ```json\n183: {\n184:   \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n185:   \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n186:   \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n187:   \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n188:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n189: }\n190: ```\n191: \n192: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n193: \n194: ### Blocked-Stop Event\n195: \n196: When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n197: \n198: ```json\n199: {\n200:   \"type\": \"event\",\n201:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n202:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n203:   \"run\": 4,\n204:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n205:   \"gateResults\": {\n206:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n207:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n208:       \"pass\": false,\n209:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n210:       \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n211:     },\n212:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n213:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n214:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n215:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n216:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n217:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n218:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n219:   },\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md, lines 100-219\n100: \n101: | Required Field | Type | Description |\n102: |---------------|------|-------------|\n103: | mode | `\"review\"` | Session mode discriminator |\n104: | dimensions | string[] | Review dimensions addressed this iteration |\n105: | filesReviewed | string[] | Files examined |\n106: | sessionId | string | Current lineage session identifier |\n107: | generation | number | Lineage generation number |\n108: | lineageMode | string | Lifecycle mode used for this run |\n109: | findingsSummary | object | Total active findings: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n110: | findingsNew | object | Net-new findings this iteration: `{ P0, P1, P2 }` |\n111: | findingDetails | array | Active findings with `id`, `severity`, `title`, `dimension`, `file`, `evidence`, `recommendation`, `disposition`, `findingClass`, `scopeProof`, and `affectedSurfaceHints`, use `[]` when there are no findings |\n112: | newFindingsRatio | number | Severity-weighted new findings ratio (0.0-1.0) |\n113: \n114: ### Convergence Signals\n115: \n116: | Signal | Weight | Description |\n117: |--------|--------|-------------|\n118: | rollingAvg | 0.30 | Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings |\n119: | madScore | 0.25 | Noise-floor test against MAD-derived churn |\n120: | dimensionCoverage | 0.45 | Required dimension + protocol coverage stability |\n121: | compositeStop | -- | Weighted stop score (stop if > 0.60) |\n122: \n123: **Severity math:** `refinementMultiplier: 0.5`, `p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50`, `noFindingsRatio: 0.0`\n124: \n125: ### Graph Events\n126: \n127: The optional `graphEvents` array records coverage graph mutations emitted by a review iteration. The workflow projects them into graph nodes and edges, and the runtime upsert script (`runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs`) persists them into `deep-loop-graph.sqlite`, where they become the source of truth for graph-assisted convergence, hotspot saturation, and blocked-stop evidence.\n128: \n129: ```json\n130: {\n131:   \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n132:   \"focus\": \"correctness\",\n133:   \"dimensions\": [\"correctness\"],\n134:   \"filesReviewed\": [\"src/api/session.ts\"],\n135:   \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n136:   \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 0 },\n137:   \"newFindingsRatio\": 0.18,\n138:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n139:   \"generation\": 1,\n140:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n141:   \"graphEvents\": [\n142:     { \"type\": \"dimension\", \"id\": \"d-correctness\", \"label\": \"correctness\" },\n143:     { \"type\": \"file\", \"id\": \"file-session-ts\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts\" },\n144:     { \"type\": \"finding\", \"id\": \"f-001\", \"label\": \"Missing CSRF token check on session POST\" },\n145:     { \"type\": \"evidence\", \"id\": \"ev-001\", \"label\": \"src/api/session.ts:42\" },\n146:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-dim-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_DIMENSION\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"d-correctness\" },\n147:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-in-file-f-001\", \"relation\": \"IN_FILE\", \"source\": \"f-001\", \"target\": \"file-session-ts\" },\n148:     { \"type\": \"edge\", \"id\": \"e-evidence-f-001\", \"relation\": \"EVIDENCE_FOR\", \"source\": \"ev-001\", \"target\": \"f-001\" }\n149:   ],\n150:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T10:12:00Z\",\n151:   \"durationMs\": 51000\n152: }\n153: ```\n154: \n155: #### Event payload shape\n156: \n157: | Field | Type | Required | Description |\n158: |-------|------|----------|-------------|\n159: | type | `\"dimension\"` \\| `\"file\"` \\| `\"finding\"` \\| `\"evidence\"` \\| `\"remediation\"` \\| `\"edge\"` | Yes | Review-loop node kind or the literal `\"edge\"` for relation rows |\n160: | id | string | Yes | Caller-chosen logical id. Must be unique **within** a single `(specFolder, loopType, sessionId)` namespace, see Namespace Rules below |\n161: | label | string | Yes | Human-readable name/caption (dimension, path, finding title, evidence anchor, etc.) |\n162: | relation | `\"COVERS\"` \\| `\"EVIDENCE_FOR\"` \\| `\"CONTRADICTS\"` \\| `\"RESOLVES\"` \\| `\"CONFIRMS\"` \\| `\"ESCALATES\"` \\| `\"IN_DIMENSION\"` \\| `\"IN_FILE\"` | edges only | Review relation type. Required when `type == \"edge\"` |\n163: | source | string | edges only | `id` of the source node inside the current namespace |\n164: | target | string | edges only | `id` of the target node inside the current namespace. Self-loops are rejected by the upsert handler |\n165: | metadata | object | No | Optional free-form metadata persisted alongside the row (e.g. `{ \"hotspot_score\": 2 }`) |\n166: \n167: #### Namespace Rules (REQ-028, REQ-029)\n168: \n169: `graphEvents` entries are scoped by the session that emits them. The coverage graph DB uses a composite primary key of `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)`, so two independent review sessions in the same spec folder MAY reuse the same logical `id` without collision, each session gets its own row.\n170: \n171: Concrete obligations for producers:\n172: \n173: 1. **Session-local uniqueness**: within one session, an `id` must resolve to exactly one node (or edge) for its entire lifetime. Re-emitting the same `id` is an upsert against the existing row in that session only.\n174: 2. **No cross-session global uniqueness requirement**: callers MUST NOT prefix ids with the session id or random salt to \"avoid collisions\". The DB layer handles namespace isolation. Salting ids only makes provenance harder to read.\n175: 3. **Edge source/target locality**: `source` and `target` in an edge event must name nodes already present in the same namespace. Cross-session edges are not a supported shape.\n176: 4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n177: \n178: The composite key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` enforces this contract directly: two sessions upsert identical node and edge ids, and both rows survive independently.\n179: \n180: ### Synthesis Event\n181: \n182: ```json\n183: {\n184:   \"type\": \"event\", \"event\": \"synthesis_complete\", \"mode\": \"review\",\n185:   \"totalIterations\": 6, \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n186:   \"activeP0\": 0, \"activeP1\": 0, \"activeP2\": 2,\n187:   \"dimensionCoverage\": 1.0, \"stopReason\": \"composite_converged\",\n188:   \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\"\n189: }\n190: ```\n191: \n192: **Required:** `type`, `event`, `mode`, `totalIterations`, `verdict`, `activeP0`, `activeP1`, `activeP2`, `dimensionCoverage`, `stopReason`, `timestamp`\n193: \n194: ### Blocked-Stop Event\n195: \n196: When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, append a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\n197: \n198: ```json\n199: {\n200:   \"type\": \"event\",\n201:   \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n202:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n203:   \"run\": 4,\n204:   \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n205:   \"gateResults\": {\n206:     \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n207:     \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n208:       \"pass\": false,\n209:       \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\"],\n210:       \"missing\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"]\n211:     },\n212:     \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n213:     \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.5 },\n214:     \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n215:     \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n216:     \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n217:     \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n218:     \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n219:   },\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":120}"},"time":{"start":1794857035607,"end":1794857036542}}}}
