{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857266159,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d46488001dArD7P4Dy2nTJ8","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d42d31001WIk4Hsksxh5P6p","type":"tool","id":"call_ba600965126e48de8ed97bf8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"presentation and the workflow\\|workflow against\\|link manifest\\|symlink-manifest\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --include=spec.md --include=acceptance-criteria.md --include=tasks.md --include=checklist.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:134:| REQ-006 | Review pass ten's two P1 are fixed: a single-quoted command name reads like a plain one before its refusal or question lead, and the doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test agree on the runtimes the link manifest offers |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:132:- [x] T038 Name the accepted runtimes instead of a count (`DIP`, `DIY`, `DICT`). Test first: in `DICT`, add a case asserting `DIP` holds no `outside the seven`, names `claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there` and says DSH is not offered, and that `DIY`'s `runtimes` input says DSH is not offered. Then change `A runtime name outside the seven` in `DIP` to `A runtime name outside claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin and pi or the ones already there`, add `DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no DSH row.` after that paragraph and append ` DSH is not offered, because the link manifest has no dsh row.` to the `runtimes` input of `DIY`. Verify: before the change the case fails, after it `NT $DICT` reports `fail 0`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md:182:- An unconditional symlink refusal in `compose` would refuse a linked install whose `REPO RULES.md` the run leaves `unchanged`, because `symlink-manifest.json` links that file. The refusal is limited to a path the run would create, replace or remove (T007).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md:270:| REQ-024 | `DR2-P2-001`: the install guide names the six accepted runtimes and `the ones already there` instead of \"the seven\", and says DSH is not offered because the link manifest has no DSH row. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/019-workflow-outcome-measure/spec.md:8:  - \"followed a real workflow against improvising\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/containment/quarantine/1/content/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:189:- The measure of the core need, how often a model followed a real workflow against improvising, is built in phase 019 and corrected in phase 022. It is a proxy: it counts a load of the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before the first write. The load rate over every owned run, before and final arm (source `019-workflow-outcome-measure/scratch/`): claude 4 of 16 to 6 of 16, codex 0 of 16 to not run, pi 3 of 16 to 5 of 16, devin 12 of 16 to 15 of 16, opencode 9 of 16 to 7 of 16, dsh 10 of 16 to 12 of 15. The share of runs that loaded or wrote: claude 4 of 4 to 6 of 6, codex 0 of 0, pi 3 of 7 to 5 of 6, devin 12 of 12 to 15 of 15, opencode 9 of 11 to 7 of 10, dsh 10 of 12 to 12 of 14. It counts 16 tuned rows with one run each, so it is not yet evidence of the outcome, and the operator sets any target. Phase 023 adds the range, the paired counts and the numbers on sealed rows.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-4/containment/quarantine/1/content/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:189:- The measure of the core need, how often a model followed a real workflow against improvising, is built in phase 019 and corrected in phase 022. It is a proxy: it counts a load of the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before the first write. The load rate over every owned run, before and final arm (source `019-workflow-outcome-measure/scratch/`): claude 4 of 16 to 6 of 16, codex 0 of 16 to not run, pi 3 of 16 to 5 of 16, devin 12 of 16 to 15 of 16, opencode 9 of 16 to 7 of 16, dsh 10 of 16 to 12 of 15. The share of runs that loaded or wrote: claude 4 of 4 to 6 of 6, codex 0 of 0, pi 3 of 7 to 5 of 6, devin 12 of 12 to 15 of 15, opencode 9 of 11 to 7 of 10, dsh 10 of 12 to 12 of 14. It counts 16 tuned rows with one run each, so it is not yet evidence of the outcome, and the operator sets any target. Phase 023 adds the range, the paired counts and the numbers on sealed rows.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-4/containment/quarantine/1/content/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:189:- The measure of the core need, how often a model followed a real workflow against improvising, is built in phase 019 and corrected in phase 022. It is a proxy: it counts a load of the command's or the owning skill's own workflow before the first write. The load rate over every owned run, before and final arm (source `019-workflow-outcome-measure/scratch/`): claude 4 of 16 to 6 of 16, codex 0 of 16 to not run, pi 3 of 16 to 5 of 16, devin 12 of 16 to 15 of 16, opencode 9 of 16 to 7 of 16, dsh 10 of 16 to 12 of 15. The share of runs that loaded or wrote: claude 4 of 4 to 6 of 6, codex 0 of 0, pi 3 of 7 to 5 of 6, devin 12 of 12 to 15 of 15, opencode 9 of 11 to 7 of 10, dsh 10 of 12 to 12 of 14. It c