{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857306828,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d50261002YtuNE5LXgmIvCX","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d4c56b001Amu4JsPlfL9Slc","type":"tool","id":"call_f759e06f85764139a023058c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":180,"path":".skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md, lines 180-299\n180: - **full-inventory leaves** — the entire sk-doc toolkit. `FULL_INVENTORY` is the\n181:   single explicit full-toolkit intent; no other intent enumerates the whole hub.\n182:   Fired only by an explicit \"show the full sk-doc toolkit / everything sk-doc\n183:   offers\" request.\n184: \n185: A single dominant documentation axis routes to one mode's leaf set; two clearly\n186: separate axes route to both.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n191: \n192: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above. The prose is the\n193: human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n194: router-replay parses. Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the\n195: matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n196: dual-reads to a canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json` or the hub's\n197: `leaf-aliases.json`.\n198: \n199: ```python\n200: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n201:     \"DOC_QUALITY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"documentation quality\", \"doc quality\", \"validate documentation\", \"validate a document\", \"validate this document\", \"validate markdown\", \"validation rules\", \"score this document\", \"score this doc\", \"dqi\", \"document audit\", \"fail sk-doc standards\", \"review the docs\", \"review the documentation\", \"document for clarity\", \"check the docs\", \"check the documentation\", \"audit the docs\", \"documentation review bar\", \"qua