{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857402512,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d61f5c0029MmKH6xiZED0WJ","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d5f098001AtbV57dpcyvkc2","type":"tool","id":"call_a248f5e490e54f20928c5f73","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001 — merged-12\n\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044` over the four `merged` paths of `review-scope-12.txt`; whole files read at `05475f9d044` (identical to `HEAD` for these paths). Merge comparison base: `origin/main` `640cd0a2499`.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. The focus names three obligations: the two sk-doc merges must equal `origin/main` except the branch's README phrase narrowings and the `/create:sk-skill` name, the generated intent signals must follow the router, and the doctor install contract test must check the presentation **and the workflow** against the link manifest. This iteration addressed the focus by diffing all three sk-doc files against `640cd0a2499`, by running the router-intent-signal generator in read-only `--check` mode, and by reading the changed doctor test against `symlink-manifest.json`, `doctor-install-presentation.txt` and `doctor-install.yaml`.\n- **Dimension this iteration:** correctness.\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start (`steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | correctness |\n\nIntegration surfaces read as context evidence, not as code findings: `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46,60`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The runtime-name contract test's workflow half cannot fail** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239-240` -- The test is titled \"the presentation and the workflow name the accepted runtimes instead of a count\", but only the presentation is checked against the link manifest. Its workflow half asserts `assert.doesNotMatch(WORKFLOW.inputs.runtimes, /is not offered/)`, and `inputs.runtimes` names no runtime at all -- it reads \"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46`). The names the workflow really prints live in the Ask step (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:60`: \"claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh\") and are never compared with `symlink-manifest.json`, so the title's claim holds for the workflow only by inspection, not by test.\nCase: change the Ask step's runtime list in `doctor-install.yaml:60` to drop `dsh` (or add a retired name such as `gemini`); `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` still passes, because `inputs.runtimes` contains no runtime name and no `is not offered`, while the operator prompt now disagrees with the eight-runtime link manifest.\nFinding class: correctness of a contract guard (an assertion that cannot fail for the mismatch its test names).\nScope proof: the changed lines `239-240` are this pass's only change in the reviewed file; the manifest read is the same test at `237-238`; `inputs.runtimes` is the field named at `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46`; the unchecked list is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:60`. Both workflow surfaces are the integration touchpoints the brief names, not scope expansion.\nAffected surface hints: the install contract test's runtime guard, the operator-facing Ask prompt in `doctor-install.yaml:60`, and `symlink-manifest.json` as the link manifest the brief requires both artifacts to be checked against.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:134` (REQ-006) requires \"the doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test agree on the runtimes the link manifest offers\". Membership currently agrees: the manifest carries eight runtimes (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json:5-13`), the presentation names all eight (`doctor-install-presentation.txt:78`), the workflow Ask step names all eight (`doctor-install.yaml:60`), and the test derives the name list from the manifest at `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:237-238`. The workflow leg of the agreement is not enforced by the test, which is finding 1. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The two sk-doc merged files carry no checklist rows of their own, and the doctor test change is covered by REQ-006 rather than a checklist item of packet `039`. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:203` (SKILL_CREATION keyword `/create:sk-skill`) — the only command-name change from `origin/main`; `/create:sk-skill` is a real route (`.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:7`) and `SKILL.md:29` names the same command.\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` — the generated intent-signal writer reports `added=0, orphans=0` for `sk-doc` (`node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc --json`, exit 0), so `intent_signals_generated` follows `ROUTER.md`'s `INTENT_SIGNALS`.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:237-240` — the only changed hunk in the doctor test binds the presentation to `symlink-manifest.json` and the workflow to the phrase absence described in finding 1.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Merge base is exact.** `git diff 05475f9d044 HEAD` over the four scope files is empty, so the working tree read equals the reviewed commit. The merge comparison against `640cd0a2499` therefore measures the branch's net result, not an intermediate.\n- **Version-only drift.** The sk-doc diffs against `origin/main` also carry version bumps (`ROUTER.md` 2.4.13.0 → 2.4.14.0, `SKILL.md` 2.9.16.0 → 2.10.0.0). These are release metadata, not behavioral divergence, and are the expected carrier of the phrase narrowings.\n- **Two intent lists differ by design.** `graph-metadata.json` carries 344 `intent_signals` and 326 `intent_signals_generated`. The 18 extra entries are hand-curated phrases the generator contract permits and never prunes; the generated list itself has no orphan and no missing router phrase.\n- **Historical checklist text.** `014-review-remediation/tasks.md:132` (T038) still describes the DSH \"is not offered\" sentence that the link manifest has since made obsolete. It records what was true when the task ran and is superseded by REQ-006 in packet `039`; it is not a live defect.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **sk-doc merge equality.** Every `origin/main` difference in `ROUTER.md` is one of: a version bump, one of the three README phrase narrowings (root-guide `security policy`, hook-readme `git-*`/`spec-gate` names, runtime-plugin `hook mirror readme`), or the `/create:sk-skill` keyword. `SKILL.md` differs only by version and the same command name. No unrelated main content was dropped.\n- **Router internal consistency.** `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` carry the same 26 keys, and all 134 `RESOURCE_MAP` paths resolve on disk under `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/`.\n- **Generated signals follow the router.** The generator's `--check` pass over `sk-doc` reports no missing phrase and no orphan; none of the removed phrases (`install guide`, `security policy`, `hook mirror readme`, the `git-*` hook names, `spec-gate hook readme`) survives in either intent list.\n- **Stale command name absent.** No `/create:skill` token remains in the three sk-doc files; the parent-hub `/create:skill-parent` is a different, live command.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The sk-doc merge dropped a mode.** The `INSTALL_GUIDE` intent and its resource-map entry are absent in both the merge result and `origin/main`; the removal comes from main, not from a branch edit, so it is not a merge regression. `sk-create-readme/assets/install-template.md` still exists and is listed by `leaf-manifest.json`, which is allowed because the resource map need not mirror every leaf.\n- **A dead `RESOURCE_MAP` path.** All 134 paths resolve; checked path by path.\n- **A stale `intent_signals_generated` orphan.** The generator check would fail on one; it exits 0.\n- **A second command-name divergence.** `/create:sk-skill` is the only command token changed from main, and it matches the live command file.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security.\n- Focus area: the same four scope files, read for trust boundaries and disclosure: whether the merged sk-doc routing prose gained or lost any instruction that could widen a write authority, and whether the doctor contract test reads any operator- or environment-controlled path without a boundary.\n- Reason: rotation to the second dimension; the correctness pass found one P2 and no blocking surface.\n- Required evidence: file:line for every claim, and the generator's exit status as the mechanical signal for the router/intent pair.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001 — merged-12\\n\\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044` over the four `merged` paths of `review-scope-12.txt`; whole files read at `05475f9d044` (identical to `HEAD` for these paths). Merge comparison base: `origin/main` `640cd0a2499`.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. The focus names three obligations: the two sk-doc merges must equal `origin/main` except the branch's README phrase narrowings and the `/create:sk-skill` name, the generated intent signals must follow the router, and the doctor install contract test must check the presentation **and the workflow** against the link manifest. This iteration addressed the focus by diffing all three sk-doc files against `640cd0a2499`, by running the router-intent-signal generator in read-only `--check` mode, and by reading the changed doctor test against `symlink-manifest.json`, `doctor-install-presentation.txt` and `doctor-install.yaml`.\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** correctness.\\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start (`steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory).\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | correctness |\\n\\nIntegration surfaces read as context evidence, not as code findings: `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46,60`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The runtime-name contract test's workflow half cannot fail** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239-240` -- The test is titled \\\"the presentation and the workflow name the accepted runtimes instead of a count\\\", but only the presentation is checked against the link manifest. Its workflow half asserts `assert.doesNotMatch(WORKFLOW.inputs.runtimes, /is not offered/)`, and `inputs.runtimes` names no runtime at all -- it reads \\\"The runtime list, supplied with --runtimes or in the consolidated prompt; the operator can choose the runtimes already there.\\\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46`). The names the workflow really prints live in the Ask step (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:60`: \\\"claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh\\\") and are never compared with `symlink-manifest.json`, so the title's claim holds for the workflow only by inspection, not by test.\\nCase: change the Ask step's runtime list in `doctor-install.yaml:60` to drop `dsh` (or add a retired name such as `gemini`); `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` still passes, because `inputs.runtimes` contains no runtime name and no `is not offered`, while the operator prompt now disagrees with the eight-runtime link manifest.\\nFinding class: correctness of a contract guard (an assertion that cannot fail for the mismatch its test names).\\nScope proof: the changed lines `239-240` are this pass's only change in the reviewed file; the manifest read is the same test at `237-238`; `inputs.runtimes` is the field named at `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:46`; the unchecked list is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:60`. Both workflow surfaces are the integration touchpoints the brief names, not scope expansion.\\nAffected surface hints: the install contract test's runtime guard, the operator-facing Ask prompt in `doctor-install.yaml:60`, and `symlink-manifest.json` as the link manifest the brief requires both artifacts to be checked against.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/spec.md:134` (REQ-006) requires \\\"the doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test agree on the runtimes the link manifest offers\\\". Membership currently agrees: the manifest carries eight runtimes (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json:5-13`), the presentation names all eight (`doctor-install-presentation.txt:78`), the workflow Ask step names all eight (`doctor-install.yaml:60`), and the test derives the name list from the manifest at `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:237-238`. The workflow leg of the agreement is not enforced by the test, which is finding 1. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The two sk-doc merged files carry no checklist rows of their own, and the doctor test change is covered by REQ-006 rather than a checklist item of packet `039`. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:203` (SKILL_CREATION keyword `/create:sk-skill`) — the only command-name change from `origin/main`; `/create:sk-skill` is a real route (`.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:7`) and `SKILL.md:29` names the same command.\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` — the generated intent-signal writer reports `added=0, orphans=0` for `sk-doc` (`node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc --json`, exit 0), so `intent_signals_generated` follows `ROUTER.md`'s `INTENT_SIGNALS`.\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:237-240` — the only changed hunk in the doctor test binds the presentation to `symlink-manifest.json` and the workflow to the phrase absence described in finding 1.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Merge base is exact.** `git diff 05475f9d044 HEAD` over the four scope files is empty, so the working tree read equals the reviewed commit. The merge comparison against `640cd0a2499` therefore measures the branch's net result, not an intermediate.\\n- **Version-only drift.** The sk-doc diffs against `origin/main` also carry version bumps (`ROUTER.md` 2.4.13.0 → 2.4.14.0, `SKILL.md` 2.9.16.0 → 2.10.0.0). These are release metadata, not behavioral divergence, and are the expected carrier of the phrase narrowings.\\n- **Two intent lists differ by design.** `graph-metadata.json` carries 344 `intent_signals` and 326 `intent_signals_generated`. The 18 extra entries are hand-curated phrases the generator contract permits and never prunes; the generated list itself has no orphan and no missing router phrase.\\n- **Historical checklist text.** `014-review-remediation/tasks.md:132` (T038) still describes the DSH \\\"is not offered\\\" sentence that the link manifest has since made obsolete. It records what was true when the task ran and is superseded by REQ-006 in packet `039`; it is not a live defect.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **sk-doc merge equality.** Every `origin/main` difference in `ROUTER.md` is one of: a version bump, one of the three README phrase narrowings (root-guide `security policy`, hook-readme `git-*`/`spec-gate` names, runtime-plugin `hook mirror readme`), or the `/create:sk-skill` keyword. `SKILL.md` differs only by version and the same command name. No unrelated main content was dropped.\\n- **Router internal consistency.** `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` carry the same 26 keys, and all 134 `RESOURCE_MAP` paths resolve on disk under `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/`.\\n- **Generated signals follow the router.** The generator's `--check` pass over `sk-doc` reports no missing phrase and no orphan; none of the removed phrases (`install guide`, `security policy`, `hook mirror readme`, the `git-*` hook names, `spec-gate hook readme`) survives in either intent list.\\n- **Stale command name absent.** No `/create:skill` token remains in the three sk-doc files; the parent-hub `/create:skill-parent` is a different, live command.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The sk-doc merge dropped a mode.** The `INSTALL_GUIDE` intent and its resource-map entry are absent in both the merge result and `origin/main`; the removal comes from main, not from a branch edit, so it is not a merge regression. `sk-create-readme/assets/install-template.md` still exists and is listed by `leaf-manifest.json`, which is allowed because the resource map need not mirror every leaf.\\n- **A dead `RESOURCE_MAP` path.** All 134 paths resolve; checked path by path.\\n- **A stale `intent_signals_generated` orphan.** The generator check would fail on one; it exits 0.\\n- **A second command-name divergence.** `/create:sk-skill` is the only command token changed from main, and it matches the live command file.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security.\\n- Focus area: the same four scope files, read for trust boundaries and disclosure: whether the merged sk-doc routing prose gained or lost any instruction that could widen a write authority, and whether the doctor contract test reads any operator- or environment-controlled path without a boundary.\\n- Reason: rotation to the second dimension; the correctness pass found one P2 and no blocking surface.\\n- Required evidence: file:line for every claim, and the generator's exit status as the mechanical signal for the router/intent pair.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857377628,"end":1794857402512}}}}
