{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857600321,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d94ef2001Z8rPsJdmJXt1jk","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d93950001Tfd5Op2Y0C4kiy","type":"tool","id":"call_a838abb471e74c0f93e1f0ea","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002 — merged-12\n\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044`; whole files at `05475f9d044`.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. This iteration read the same three obligations through the security dimension: whether any merged sk-doc text widens a write authority or drops a guard, and whether the changed doctor test opens an operator- or environment-controlled path. It also re-ran the two mechanical router checks the packet names (REQ-005).\n- **Dimension this iteration:** security.\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | security |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | security |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | security |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | security |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | REQ-005's mechanical pair passes: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with \"SIGNAL DRIFT compiled vs disk: none\" and \"(report-only ... nothing was written)\", and `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc --json` reports `added=0, orphans=0`. REQ-006 stays partial for the same workflow-leg reason recorded in iteration 1. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No checklist row governs a security property of these four files. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:4` — `allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]` is identical to `origin/main`; the merge changed no authority grant.\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` — every hunk versus `640cd0a2499` is prose tightening, a keyword removal, or the command rename; none adds an instruction to write, execute, or fetch.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:17-25` — all paths are `__dirname`-relative constants (`DOCTOR`, `ASSETS`, `CONTRACT_ASSETS`); the test reads local files and parses YAML in-process, with no `child_process`, no network call, and no environment-controlled path.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Instruction surface of a router.** `ROUTER.md` is read as instructions by a model, so a merge can widen authority without changing code. Checked by diffing the whole file against main: no such hunk exists.\n- **YAML parsing in the test.** `parseYaml` reads repository-owned assets only, so the parse is not a trust boundary; a malformed asset fails the suite rather than executing anything.\n- **Report-only tooling.** `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` states it writes nothing; its exit 0 is used only as evidence for REQ-005, not as a mutation.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **No authority widening.** The merged sk-doc files grant the same tools as main; the only control-flow change is the command name a keyword points at.\n- **No secret or absolute-path exposure.** `graph-metadata.json` carries intent phrases and skill metadata only; no token, path, or environment value was added by the merge.\n- **No write path in the test.** The doctor contract test performs reads and in-memory assertions only; the `_routes.yaml` and `symlink-manifest.json` reads are fixed local paths.\n- **No hidden instruction in the reviewed text.** The files contain routing prose, not operational directives that would let a reviewed artifact redirect the reviewer.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The narrowing removes a security guard.** The removed phrases are README intent keywords (`security policy`, the `git-*` hook README names, `hook mirror readme`); the `SECURITY_POLICY` intent still fires on `security.md` and its template stays mapped at `ROUTER.md:298-300`.\n- **A test-side path injection.** No reviewed test input is caller-supplied; all reads resolve under `__dirname`.\n- **A shell surface added by the test diff.** The changed hunk adds one `assert.doesNotMatch`, with no spawn or eval.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability.\n- Focus area: map each merged file's observable content to REQ-005 and REQ-006 of packet `039`, and check the doctor test's checklist evidence against the merged workflow and presentation. Carry the iteration 1 P2 only if a new input shows it is wider.\n- Reason: rotation to the third dimension; security produced no new finding.\n- Required evidence: spec path:line, test path:line, and the two tool exit statuses already captured.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002 — merged-12\\n\\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044`; whole files at `05475f9d044`.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. This iteration read the same three obligations through the security dimension: whether any merged sk-doc text widens a write authority or drops a guard, and whether the changed doctor test opens an operator- or environment-controlled path. It also re-ran the two mechanical router checks the packet names (REQ-005).\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** security.\\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | security |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | security |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | security |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | security |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | REQ-005's mechanical pair passes: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 with \\\"SIGNAL DRIFT compiled vs disk: none\\\" and \\\"(report-only ... nothing was written)\\\", and `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc --json` reports `added=0, orphans=0`. REQ-006 stays partial for the same workflow-leg reason recorded in iteration 1. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | No checklist row governs a security property of these four files. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md:4` — `allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]` is identical to `origin/main`; the merge changed no authority grant.\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` — every hunk versus `640cd0a2499` is prose tightening, a keyword removal, or the command rename; none adds an instruction to write, execute, or fetch.\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:17-25` — all paths are `__dirname`-relative constants (`DOCTOR`, `ASSETS`, `CONTRACT_ASSETS`); the test reads local files and parses YAML in-process, with no `child_process`, no network call, and no environment-controlled path.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Instruction surface of a router.** `ROUTER.md` is read as instructions by a model, so a merge can widen authority without changing code. Checked by diffing the whole file against main: no such hunk exists.\\n- **YAML parsing in the test.** `parseYaml` reads repository-owned assets only, so the parse is not a trust boundary; a malformed asset fails the suite rather than executing anything.\\n- **Report-only tooling.** `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` states it writes nothing; its exit 0 is used only as evidence for REQ-005, not as a mutation.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **No authority widening.** The merged sk-doc files grant the same tools as main; the only control-flow change is the command name a keyword points at.\\n- **No secret or absolute-path exposure.** `graph-metadata.json` carries intent phrases and skill metadata only; no token, path, or environment value was added by the merge.\\n- **No write path in the test.** The doctor contract test performs reads and in-memory assertions only; the `_routes.yaml` and `symlink-manifest.json` reads are fixed local paths.\\n- **No hidden instruction in the reviewed text.** The files contain routing prose, not operational directives that would let a reviewed artifact redirect the reviewer.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The narrowing removes a security guard.** The removed phrases are README intent keywords (`security policy`, the `git-*` hook README names, `hook mirror readme`); the `SECURITY_POLICY` intent still fires on `security.md` and its template stays mapped at `ROUTER.md:298-300`.\\n- **A test-side path injection.** No reviewed test input is caller-supplied; all reads resolve under `__dirname`.\\n- **A shell surface added by the test diff.** The changed hunk adds one `assert.doesNotMatch`, with no spawn or eval.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability.\\n- Focus area: map each merged file's observable content to REQ-005 and REQ-006 of packet `039`, and check the doctor test's checklist evidence against the merged workflow and presentation. Carry the iteration 1 P2 only if a new input shows it is wider.\\n- Reason: rotation to the third dimension; security produced no new finding.\\n- Required evidence: spec path:line, test path:line, and the two tool exit statuses already captured.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857586418,"end":1794857600321}}}}
