{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857612951,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5d9b68d002j6P6vS9qyyEUfr","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5d9ae46001vJtrbcs5V3zhLH","type":"tool","id":"call_994f176ef18a41698c9c52de","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/deep-review-strategy.md","limit":140},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-140\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - merged-12\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: ### Purpose\n6: \n7: Persistent review state for the detached fan-out lineage `merged-12` of review pass twelve on `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\n8: \n9: ### Usage\n10: \n11: - Per iteration: read Next Focus, review the assigned dimension/files, update findings, mark dimensions complete, and set the next focus.\n12: - Mutability: mutable inside this lineage directory only.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 2. TOPIC\n17: \n18: Review of the two merges of `origin/main` (`640cd0a2499`) into the command-surfacing branch: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` and `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` must equal main except the branch's README phrase narrowings and the `/create:sk-skill` command name; the generated intent signals must follow the router; and `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` must check the presentation and the workflow against the link manifest.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n23: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n24: - [ ] security\n25: - [ ] traceability\n26: - [ ] maintainability\n27: \n28: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n29: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n30: \n31: - Re-reporting the recorded limits named in `review/review-brief-12.txt` (suffix-plus-extension reads as command, `node -e` arrow redirect, macOS-only isolation check, underscore emphasis, moved baseline rows judged without text, the open P2 list of `038-alignment-p1-remediation/scratch/alignment-final-dispositions.md`, and the open P2 of review passes ten and eleven).\n32: - Re-reviewing the `mention` area (`command-attach.ts` and its guards) except where a merged-file claim depends on it.\n33: - Reading or printing holdout fixture content; the holdout gate is read by count only.\n34: \n35: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n36: \n37: - `config.stopPolicy: convergence` with `config.convergenceThreshold: 0.1` and `config.maxIterations: 8`, whichever the `convergence.cjs` stop decision reaches first.\n38: - A failed required quality gate (evidence, scope, coverage) blocks STOP and must be answered or reported.\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n43: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n44: - [x] correctness\n45: \n46: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n47: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n48: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n49: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n50: - P1 (Required): 0\n51: - P2 (Suggestions): 1\n52: - Resolved: 0\n53: \n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n55: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n56: \n57: - Diffing each merged sk-doc file against `origin/main 640cd0a2499` and classifying every hunk (iteration 1): it makes \"only the narrowings and the rename differ\" a checkable claim instead of a reading.\n58: - Running `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check --hub sk-doc --json` (iteration 1): it converts the router-versus-intent-signal obligation into one mechanical result (`added=0, orphans=0`).\n59: \n60: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n61: \n62: - Reading the doctor contract-test title as evidence of its assertions (iteration 1): the workflow half asserts a phrase that the inspected field could never contain, so the title over-claims. The failure is now recorded as the iteration 1 P2.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n67: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n68: ### **A dead `RESOURCE_MAP` path.** All 134 paths resolve; checked path by path. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n69: - What was tried: **A dead `RESOURCE_MAP` path.** All 134 paths resolve; checked path by path.\n70: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n71: - Do NOT retry: **A dead `RESOURCE_MAP` path.** All 134 paths resolve; checked path by path.\n72: \n73: ### **A second command-name divergence.** `/create:sk-skill` is the only command token changed from main, and it matches the live command file. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n74: - What was tried: **A second command-name divergence.** `/create:sk-skill` is the only command token changed from main, and it matches the live command file.\n75: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n76: - Do NOT retry: **A second command-name divergence.** `/create:sk-skill` is the only command token changed from main, and it matches the live command file.\n77: \n78: ### **A stale `intent_signals_generated` orphan.** The generator check would fail on one; it exits 0. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n79: - What was tried: **A stale `intent_signals_generated` orphan.** The generator check would fail on one; it exits 0.\n80: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n81: - Do NOT retry: **A stale `intent_signals_generated` orphan.** The generator check would fail on one; it exits 0.\n82: \n83: ### **The sk-doc merge dropped a mode.** The `INSTALL_GUIDE` intent and its resource-map entry are absent in both the merge result and `origin/main`; the removal comes from main, not from a branch edit, so it is not a merge regression. `sk-create-readme/assets/install-template.md` still exists and is listed by `leaf-manifest.json`, which is allowed because the resource map need not mirror every leaf. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n84: - What was tried: **The sk-doc merge dropped a mode.** The `INSTALL_GUIDE` intent and its resource-map entry are absent in both the merge result and `origin/main`; the removal comes from main, not from a branch edit, so it is not a merge regression. `sk-create-readme/assets/install-template.md` still exists and is listed by `leaf-manifest.json`, which is allowed because the resource map need not mirror every leaf.\n85: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n86: - Do NOT retry: **The sk-doc merge dropped a mode.** The `INSTALL_GUIDE` intent and its resource-map entry are absent in both the merge result and `origin/main`; the removal comes from main, not from a branch edit, so it is not a merge regression. `sk-create-readme/assets/install-template.md` still exists and is listed by `leaf-manifest.json`, which is allowed because the resource map need not mirror every leaf.\n87: \n88: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n89: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n90: - Completed pivots: 0\n91: - Failed pivots: 0\n92: - Audited overrides: 0\n93: - Swept: none yet\n94: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n95: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n96: \n97: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n98: \n99: [Review angles investigated and eliminated]\n100: \n101: ---\n102: \n103: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n104: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n105: - Dimension: security. - Focus area: the same four scope files, read for trust boundaries and disclosure: whether the merged sk-doc routing prose gained or lost any instruction that could widen a write authority, and whether the doctor contract test reads any operator- or environment-controlled path without a boundary. - Reason: rotation to the second dimension; the correctness pass found one P2 and no blocking surface. - Required evidence: file:line for every claim, and the generator's exit status as the mechanical signal for the router/intent pair. Review verdict: PASS\n106: \n107: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n108: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEX