y, and the prose says why |\n69:| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n70:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modified | Recompiled graph |\n72:| `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and its guards test | Modified | A single quote that opens or closes a command name is dropped before the lead reading, and a retired name reads beside its replacement, from review passes ten and eleven. One test pins that every mention fixture reads the same wrapped or retired as plain |\n73:| Doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test | Modified | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence, from review pass ten |\n107:| Intent signals and graph freshness | PASS, `--check` RESULT: PASSED and `--strict` exit 0 |\n117:2. **A README request for a `git-*` or `spec-gate` hook or for a hook mirror folder loads the generic README template.** sk-doc still owns the request, but the hook and runtime plugin templates no longer load for those names. Asking for \"a README for this hook\" still loads the hook template.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n -i \\\"workflow\\\\|runtime\\\\|symlink-manifest\\\\|contract test\\\\|graph-metadata\\\\|intent signal\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/implementation-summary.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857725970,"end":1794857727658}}}}
