{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794857927990,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5de488b0022jI8dr5LL66vcl","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5de2b59001HwxmpFiX8uUyAu","type":"tool","id":"call_98558668d207476cb3d454db","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004 — merged-12\n\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044`; whole files at `05475f9d044`.\n**Recovery mode:** iteration 3's stop pass returned `stuckRecovery` (`stuckThresholdReached`); this pass changes granularity to line-level reading and re-runs the severity escalation review of the open P2, per the workflow's recovery strategies.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. This iteration read the same obligations through the maintainability dimension: whether the narrowing rationale is legible where a future editor will look, whether a test title, comment or generated list claims more than it enforces, and whether the changed assertion's cost is safe to modify.\n- **Dimension this iteration:** maintainability (recovery granularity).\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | maintainability |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. The recovery severity review of `MRG12-P2-001` keeps it at P2: the mismatch is currently latent (all three doctor artifacts agree), the guard is the only defect, and no input reaches a wrong operator action today. Escalation to P1 would require a shown live desync between `doctor-install.yaml:60` and `symlink-manifest.json:5-13`; none exists.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: REQ-005 passes both mechanical checks; REQ-006's workflow leg is unenforced by the test. The maintainability pass adds no new code-to-spec divergence. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md:65` still describes more than `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:240` does; recorded, not re-filed. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:127-134` — the three narrowing sentences state the reason next to the removal (\"it pulled a request that was not a README into this skill\", \"their names carry git, hooks and gate\", \"'mirror' belongs to the runtime mirror doctor\"), so a future editor can re-derive the boundary without the review history.\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:195-197` — the machine-readable block states the sync obligation and that every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves through `leaf-manifest.json`; both properties were re-verified in this run.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:234-237` — the test's own name states the contract it means to enforce; the assertion at `:240` is the half that does not reach it. This is the open P2's maintainability face, not a second finding.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Recovery changes the read, not the scope.** The granularity change re-read the same four files at line level; it did not widen the target, and the review still treats the files as read-only.\n- **Two intent lists are deliberately distinct.** `graph-metadata.json`'s 344 `intent_signals` and 326 `intent_signals_generated` are documented by the generator header as authored versus provenance; a reader who mistakes one for the other is warned by that header, so no code change is warranted.\n- **Derived block timestamps.** `graph-metadata.json`'s derived block keeps `last_updated_at: 2026-09-26T00:00:00Z`; `regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:189-216` stamps that block only when the derived content changes, and the merge changed only `intent_signals`. The timestamp is therefore correct for its field, not stale metadata.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **The narrowing rationale is durable.** Each of the three phrase removals carries its reason in the router prose, which is the file a maintainer edits.\n- **The generated block is machine-owned.** Its provenance list and orphan rule are stated in `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`'s header and enforced by `--check`; no hand-maintained duplicate needs updating.\n- **The changed test is cheap to extend.** Deriving `named` from the link manifest means a future runtime addition fails the presentation assertion first, which is the intended tripwire.\n- **The command rename is single-sourced.** `/create:sk-skill` appears in the router keyword, the SKILL.md mode table, and the live command file, with no stale `/create:skill` token left in the three merged files.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **P2 escalation to P1.** Re-read `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239-240`, `doctor-install.yaml:46,60` and `symlink-manifest.json:5-13`: the three artifacts agree today, so the defect is guard coverage only.\n- **A stale derived timestamp.** The stamp is block-scoped and the block did not change.\n- **A second drift between the two intent lists.** The generator check reports no missing phrase and no orphan.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining; all four dimensions are covered.\n- Focus area: stop decision. If convergence allows STOP, synthesize; otherwise continue with the gate named in `blockedBy`.\n- Reason: coverage completion is the precondition the graph was blocking on.\n- Required evidence: the stop decision's `blockedBy` and the coverage ratio.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004 — merged-12\\n\\n**Lineage:** `merged-12` (detached fan-out, review pass twelve, area `merged`)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12`\\n**Session:** `fanout-merged-12-1794856957949-n58dw7`\\n**Diff under review:** `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2f3f893c153 05475f9d044`; whole files at `05475f9d044`.\\n**Recovery mode:** iteration 3's stop pass returned `stuckRecovery` (`stuckThresholdReached`); this pass changes granularity to line-level reading and re-runs the severity escalation review of the open P2, per the workflow's recovery strategies.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass twelve, area `merged`, per `review/review-brief-12.txt`. This iteration read the same obligations through the maintainability dimension: whether the narrowing rationale is legible where a future editor will look, whether a test title, comment or generated list claims more than it enforces, and whether the changed assertion's cost is safe to modify.\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** maintainability (recovery granularity).\\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | maintainability |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. The recovery severity review of `MRG12-P2-001` keeps it at P2: the mismatch is currently latent (all three doctor artifacts agree), the guard is the only defect, and no input reaches a wrong operator action today. Escalation to P1 would require a shown live desync between `doctor-install.yaml:60` and `symlink-manifest.json:5-13`; none exists.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | Unchanged from iteration 3: REQ-005 passes both mechanical checks; REQ-006's workflow leg is unenforced by the test. The maintainability pass adds no new code-to-spec divergence. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair/tasks.md:65` still describes more than `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:240` does; recorded, not re-filed. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:127-134` — the three narrowing sentences state the reason next to the removal (\\\"it pulled a request that was not a README into this skill\\\", \\\"their names carry git, hooks and gate\\\", \\\"'mirror' belongs to the runtime mirror doctor\\\"), so a future editor can re-derive the boundary without the review history.\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:195-197` — the machine-readable block states the sync obligation and that every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves through `leaf-manifest.json`; both properties were re-verified in this run.\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:234-237` — the test's own name states the contract it means to enforce; the assertion at `:240` is the half that does not reach it. This is the open P2's maintainability face, not a second finding.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Recovery changes the read, not the scope.** The granularity change re-read the same four files at line level; it did not widen the target, and the review still treats the files as read-only.\\n- **Two intent lists are deliberately distinct.** `graph-metadata.json`'s 344 `intent_signals` and 326 `intent_signals_generated` are documented by the generator header as authored versus provenance; a reader who mistakes one for the other is warned by that header, so no code change is warranted.\\n- **Derived block timestamps.** `graph-metadata.json`'s derived block keeps `last_updated_at: 2026-09-26T00:00:00Z`; `regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:189-216` stamps that block only when the derived content changes, and the merge changed only `intent_signals`. The timestamp is therefore correct for its field, not stale metadata.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **The narrowing rationale is durable.** Each of the three phrase removals carries its reason in the router prose, which is the file a maintainer edits.\\n- **The generated block is machine-owned.** Its provenance list and orphan rule are stated in `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs`'s header and enforced by `--check`; no hand-maintained duplicate needs updating.\\n- **The changed test is cheap to extend.** Deriving `named` from the link manifest means a future runtime addition fails the presentation assertion first, which is the intended tripwire.\\n- **The command rename is single-sourced.** `/create:sk-skill` appears in the router keyword, the SKILL.md mode table, and the live command file, with no stale `/create:skill` token left in the three merged files.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **P2 escalation to P1.** Re-read `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239-240`, `doctor-install.yaml:46,60` and `symlink-manifest.json:5-13`: the three artifacts agree today, so the defect is guard coverage only.\\n- **A stale derived timestamp.** The stamp is block-scoped and the block did not change.\\n- **A second drift between the two intent lists.** The generator check reports no missing phrase and no orphan.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining; all four dimensions are covered.\\n- Focus area: stop decision. If convergence allows STOP, synthesize; otherwise continue with the gate named in `blockedBy`.\\n- Reason: coverage completion is the precondition the graph was blocking on.\\n- Required evidence: the stop decision's `blockedBy` and the coverage ratio.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/merged-12/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794857912459,"end":1794857927990}}}}
