{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794858212437,"sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5e2db16002p4k2vreJ6c5JPp","sessionID":"ses_e1a303974ffe7fw3NHmuXnjadA","messageID":"msg_1e5e2cbbb0010A2ScHz7UA66o4","type":"tool","id":"call_d0d020e35991417b9480d61f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 2394e8f797c^1 2394e8f797c -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md | head -140"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\nindex d5ba29d34d2..5dd2dcbf5ff 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\n@@ -249,7 +249,6 @@\n         \"/create:readme\",\n         \"readme for\",\n         \"skill readme\",\n-        \"install guide\",\n         \"contributing guide\",\n         \"contributing.md\",\n         \"security policy\",\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md\nindex 5fe41d66383..749d48b9273 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"sk-create-readme routing\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.0.4.0\n+version: 1.0.5.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ It routes to ten artifact templates under `assets/`:\n - `runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a folder a runtime loads its hooks from, or a hook mirror.\n - `runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README and its `SYNC.md`.\n - `architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n-- `install-template.md` for a repository install guide.\n - `contributing-template.md` for a repository contributing guide.\n - `security-policy-template.md` for a repository security policy.\n \n@@ -45,7 +44,7 @@ loads before an intent selects it.\n \n ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n \n-- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n+- **`readme`** fires on `readme`, `readme for`, `folder readme`, `create readme`, `write readme`, `project readme`, `skill readme`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md` and `sync doc for the` at weight 4. It selects the template the target names: `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package, `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`, a root-guide template for an install guide, contributing guide or security policy, `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a hook folder, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a plugin or extension folder, `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README or `SYNC.md`, and `assets/readme-template.md` for everything else. It then loads the flat markdown inventory under `references/` and `assets/`.\n - **`code_readme`** fires on `code folder readme`, `source-code folder readme` and `source code readme` at weight 4. It selects `assets/readme-code-template.md` and loads the same flat inventory, with `references/readme/` carrying the extended code-folder voice and pattern detail.\n \n ---\n@@ -61,7 +60,6 @@ Route by artifact type first, then by folder purpose.\n | --- | --- | --- |\n | Repository front page, feature or component README | `README.md` in the target folder | `assets/readme-template.md` |\n | Skill package README | `README.md` at the skill package root | `assets/skill-readme-template.md` |\n-| Repository install guide | `INSTALL.md` at the repository root | `assets/install-template.md` |\n | Repository contributing guide | `CONTRIBUTING.md` at the repository root | `assets/contributing-template.md` |\n | Repository security policy | `SECURITY.md` at the repository root | `assets/security-policy-template.md` |\n | Source-code folder README | `README.md` in the source folder | `assets/readme-code-template.md` |\n@@ -106,7 +104,7 @@ DEFAULT_RESOURCE = \"references/README.md\"\n \n # Two output artifacts; keywords come from this packet's activation triggers.\n INTENT_MODEL = {\n-    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"install guide\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n+    \"readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"readme\", \"readme for\", \"folder readme\", \"create readme\", \"write readme\", \"project readme\", \"skill readme\", \"contributing guide\", \"security policy\", \"sync.md\", \"sync doc for the\"]},\n     \"code_readme\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"code folder readme\", \"source-code folder readme\", \"source code readme\"]},\n }\n UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md\nindex d2f492f6885..2d2d5051d0c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md\n@@ -20,12 +20,12 @@ Use this packet when the request involves:\n - Creating or refreshing a folder `README.md`.\n - Documenting a project, skill, feature, component or source-code directory.\n - Writing a skill package's README, including the README step `create-skill` hands over while it scaffolds a new skill.\n-- Writing a repository's front page, install guide, contributing guide or security policy.\n+- Writing a repository's front page, contributing guide or security policy.\n - Writing developer orientation for a code folder, including topology, boundaries, entrypoints and validation.\n - Writing the README of a hook folder, a runtime plugin or extension folder, or a runtime folder and its `SYNC.md`.\n - Running `/create:readme`.\n \n-Keyword triggers: `create readme`, `/create:readme`, `readme`, `folder readme`, `write readme`, `README.md`, `front-page overview`, `code folder readme`, `skill readme`, `install guide`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md`, `sync doc for the`.\n+Keyword triggers: `create readme`, `/create:readme`, `readme`, `folder readme`, `write readme`, `README.md`, `front-page overview`, `code folder readme`, `skill readme`, `contributing guide`, `security policy`, `sync.md`, `sync doc for the`.\n \n ### When NOT to Use\n \n@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ The hub's mode signal selects this packet.\n The artifact decides the template before the folder decides the sections.\n \n Authoring starts from the matching template: `assets/readme-template.md` for a repository front page or a general README, `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package README, `assets/readme-code-template.md` for a source-code folder and `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n-A repository's root guides start from `assets/install-template.md`, `assets/contributing-template.md` and `assets/security-policy-template.md`.\n+A repository's root guides start from `assets/contributing-template.md` and `assets/security-policy-template.md`.\n Hook code starts from its own scaffolds: `assets/hook-readme-template.md` for a shared hook folder and its runtime adapter folders, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` for a folder a runtime loads its hooks from and `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for a runtime folder's README and `SYNC.md`.\n `references/README.md` is the fallback route map when the artifact type or folder purpose is unclear.\n \n@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@ The core workflow lives in this `SKILL.md`. Use these files only for deep overfl\n \n - `assets/readme-template.md` for the selection guide, the general README scaffold and the front-page scaffold.\n - `assets/skill-readme-template.md` for a skill package README, the template `create-skill` hands the README step to.\n-- `assets/install-template.md`, `assets/contributing-template.md` and `assets/security-policy-template.md` for a repository's root guides.\n+- `assets/contributing-template.md` and `assets/security-policy-template.md` for a repository's root guides.\n - `assets/readme-code-template.md` for the full fillable code-folder scaffold and diagram examples.\n - `assets/hook-readme-template.md`, `assets/runtime-plugin-readme-template.md` and `assets/runtime-folder-template.md` for hook folders, the runtime folders that load them and a runtime folder's README and `SYNC.md`.\n - `assets/architecture-template.md` for a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`: the fixed eight-section system document.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\nindex d5ba29d34d2..5dd2dcbf5ff 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json\n@@ -249,7 +249,6 @@\n         \"/create:readme\",\n         \"readme for\",\n         \"skill readme\",\n-        \"install guide\",\n         \"contributing guide\",\n         \"contributi